SUMMARY:Tuesday Fitness Ride 25R (17-19 mph)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nAverage speed: 17-19 mph\
 n\nThis ride has been added to the LBC ride calendar in order to provide a
  time and place during the week for working people to build fitness on an 
 evening ride throughout the spring\, summer and early fall months. In LBC 
 nomenclature\, this is a B/B+ ride level. This new ride will attempt to re
 duce the barriers that exist about joining the Tu/Th evening rides by a cr
 eating medium-paced group.\n\n25 mile rolling route:\n\nOdd dates: CC Tues
 day Fitness Ride Odd Days (25R)\nEven dates: CC Tuesday Fitness Ride Even 
 Days (26R)\n\nFor links to both cues:\n[https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.n
 et/?l=7&t&c&mi&k=tuesday%20fitness](https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/?
 l=7&t&c&mi&k=tuesday%20fitness)\n\nBring lights as needed\; Helmets are ma
 ndatory\; No ear buds. Please bring water\, and a basic repair kit (spare 
 tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nHelmets are mandatory\; No ear
  buds or audible music playing devices. Please bring water\, and a basic r
 epair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate 
 passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require LBC Club membership and
  Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on Meetup does not mean you ar
 e a club member.\nJoin here [Member Signup](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.
 net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nYour RSVP is your agreement t
 o abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of Conduct](https://www.lanca
 sterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\nGuidance if an i
 ncident occurs: [Incident Actions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.a
 spx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=326137)i
